  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $⟨2,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+ky=5 \\\\ x+2y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
